//RS 
//RS /// U9 remote probe: classify an `…@github`/git upstream as `Core` (it carries a
//RS /// `package.jet` or migration-era `pkg.jet`) or `Nix` (it does not), peeking
//RS /// **only** the root package marker — never
//RS /// cloning a nixpkgs-sized repo just to classify it.
//RS ///
//RS /// Resolution order:
//RS /// 1. If a source-cache checkout already exists (a prior realize fetched it),
//RS ///    classify from the local tree — offline-safe, no network.
//RS /// 2. Offline with no cache: we can't probe, so default to `nix`.
//RS /// 3. Online: a lightweight `git` peek — a partial, no-checkout, depth-1 clone
//RS ///    (`--filter=tree:0`, so blobs/subtrees are never downloaded) into a temp
//RS ///    dir, then `git ls-tree <rev> package.jet pkg.jet`. Present → `Core`;
